From: Jordan Bettcher <thebettcher@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] linux: link plugin libraries with RUNPATH $ORIGIN, not the build tree

Class:   UPSTREAMABLE FIX (to Flutter's Linux app template,
         packages/flutter_tools/templates/app/linux.tmpl/CMakeLists.txt.tmpl,
         which LocalSend's app/linux/CMakeLists.txt is generated from; every
         Flutter Linux app with plugins has it).
Applies: localsend v1.18.2 (patch -p1 from the repository root), after 0003.
Fixes:   the bundle's plugin libraries are copied with install(FILES), so
         they keep CMake's build RUNPATH: the absolute
         <build tree>/app/linux/flutter/ephemeral directory. Measured on the
         M8 bundle: all 12 plugin .so files carried
         RUNPATH [/mnt/arch/.../app/linux/flutter/ephemeral]. In a package
         that is a build path in every installed plugin and a library search
         path into whatever directory later exists there. With this change
         they carry RUNPATH [$ORIGIN] (libflutter_linux_gtk.so is beside them
         in lib/); the runner keeps $ORIGIN/lib (install(TARGETS) rewrites
         it), and FFI plugins' prebuilt libraries are not linked here.
---
--- a/app/linux/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/app/linux/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -97,6 +97,16 @@
 # them to the application.
 include(flutter/generated_plugins.cmake)
 
+# Plugin libraries reach the bundle through install(FILES), which keeps the
+# RUNPATH they were linked with: CMake's build RUNPATH, the absolute
+# flutter/ephemeral directory of the build tree. Link them with the install
+# RUNPATH instead; libflutter_linux_gtk.so sits next to them in lib/.
+foreach(plugin ${FLUTTER_PLUGIN_LIST})
+  set_target_properties(${plugin}_plugin PROPERTIES
+    BUILD_WITH_INSTALL_RPATH TRUE
+    INSTALL_RPATH "$ORIGIN")
+endforeach(plugin)
+
 
 # === Installation ===
 # By default, "installing" just makes a relocatable bundle in the build
